# Deploy gate checklist: <service> <release or digest>

Fill one copy per production promotion. Every "no" needs a named owner's
written exception before the promotion continues.

## Artifact

| Check | Answer | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The candidate is one immutable digest (`registry/name@sha256:...`) | yes / no | |
| The digest was built once by CI from a reviewed commit on the trunk | yes / no | CI run link |
| `gh attestation verify` passed for the digest and the CI workflow | yes / no | command output |
| The same digest already ran in every earlier environment | yes / no | deployment links |
| Vulnerability and license gates passed for this digest (`kit-supply-chain`) | yes / no | |

## Pipeline

| Check | Answer | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Required checks passed on the merge commit; none skipped by path filters | yes / no | |
| The deploy workflow passed `check_delivery_workflow.py` | yes / no | output |
| Workflow security review is current (`kit-ci-review`) | yes / no | |
| The deploy job uses OIDC with an environment-scoped subject | yes / no | |
| Deploy concurrency queues; it never cancels an in-progress deploy | yes / no | |

## Change content

| Check | Answer | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Schema changes are expand-only, or contract runs after all readers moved (`kit-database-migrations`) | yes / no / n/a | |
| New behavior ships dark behind a flag with an owner and removal date | yes / no / n/a | |
| Configuration changes are versioned with the release and reversible | yes / no / n/a | |
| Breaking API or event changes have a published migration path | yes / no / n/a | |

## Rollout

| Check | Answer | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Strategy chosen and recorded (canary, blue-green, slot swap, rolling) | | |
| Canary steps, bake time, and abort thresholds are written down | yes / no | |
| Abort signals: error ratio, latency, saturation, burn rate (`kit-observability`) | yes / no | dashboard link |
| The rollback target (revision, slot, or digest) exists and is healthy | yes / no | |
| The rollback has been exercised in a lower environment this quarter | yes / no | date |
| An on-call owner is reachable for the bake period | yes / no | name |

## Decision

- Approver (not the author of the change):
- Time window:
- Decision: promote / hold / reject
- Notes:
